{{/* theme: builtin */}}
{{ define "content" }}
<div class="page-help">
    <h1>{{T "Help"}}</h1>
    <h2>{{T "Dashboards"}}</h2>
    <p>{{T "A dashboard is a page you customize yourself - pin lists of files by tag or folder, saved searches, or your own notes, arranged however you like."}}</p>
    <p>{{T "You're seeing this help page because no home dashboard exists yet. The home dashboard is simply whichever dashboard appears on the start page - home by default, changeable in Settings."}}</p>
    <p>{{T "Create a dashboard and name it home to make it your new start page."}}</p>
    <div class="admin-links">
        <a href="/dashboard/new">{{T "New Dashboard"}}</a>
    </div>

    <h2>{{T "Files"}}</h2>
    <p>{{T "Every file has an editor type - pick the one that fits what you're writing."}}</p>
    <ul class="help-list">
        <li><a href="/files/new/codemirror">{{T "Markdown"}}</a> - {{T "distraction-free writing"}}</li>
        <li><a href="/files/new/list">{{T "List"}}</a> - {{T "drag-and-drop nested list"}}</li>
        <li><a href="/files/new/todo">{{T "Todo"}}</a> - {{T "checkbox task list"}}</li>
        <li><a href="/files/new/index">{{T "Index"}}</a> - {{T "ordered list of links to other files (a map of content)"}}</li>
        <li><a href="/files/new/filter">{{T "Filter"}}</a> - {{T "saved search, built visually"}}</li>
        <li><a href="/files/new/tracker">{{T "Tracker"}}</a> - {{T "named counters logged with +/- and shown as a stats table"}}</li>
        <li><a href="/files/new/book">{{T "Book"}}</a> - {{T "compose files and sections into one exportable document"}}</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>{{T "Links"}}</h2>
    <p>{{T "Where a link points depends on how it is written, for a link in the file sub/n.md:"}}</p>
    <ul class="help-list">
        <li><code>[x](a.md)</code>, <code>[x](./a.md)</code>, <code>[x](../a.md)</code> - {{T "from the folder of the file (sub/a.md, a.md)"}}</li>
        <li><code>[x](/a.md)</code>, <code>[x](/files/a.md)</code> - {{T "from the docs root (a.md)"}}</li>
        <li><code>[[a]]</code> - {{T "from the docs root, a wikilink is a page name (a.md)"}}</li>
        <li><code>[[./a]]</code>, <code>[[../a]]</code> - {{T "from the folder of the file"}}</li>
        <li><code>[x](media/pic.png)</code>, <code>[[media/pic.png]]</code> - {{T "from the media folder"}}</li>
        <li><code>[x](/files/media/a.md)</code>, <code>[[docs/media/a]]</code> - {{T "a docs file in a folder named docs, media or files (media/... alone is the media folder)"}}</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>{{T "Browse & Search"}}</h2>
    <p>{{T "Files can be found by where they live or by labels attached to them."}}</p>
    <ul class="help-list">
        <li><a href="/browse/folder">{{T "Folders"}}</a> - {{T "where a file lives, nested like on disk"}}</li>
        <li><a href="/browse/collection">{{T "Collections"}}</a> - {{T "a file's top-level folder, a coarser grouping"}}</li>
        <li><a href="/browse/tag">{{T "Tags"}}</a> - {{T "freeform labels, independent of location - a file can have several"}}</li>
        <li><a href="/browse/editor">{{T "Editor types"}}</a> - {{T "group files by which editor they use"}}</li>
        <li><a href="/search">{{T "Search"}}</a> - {{T "full-text search across all files"}}</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>{{T "Media"}}</h2>
    <p>{{T "Upload images and attachments straight from the editor. They show up in Browse & Search like any other file, and are versioned the same way as your notes (see History)."}}</p>
    <div class="admin-links">
        <a href="/media">{{T "Media"}}</a>
    </div>

    <h2>{{T "History"}}</h2>
    <p>{{T "Every change - to a file or a media upload - is automatically saved as a new version using git, the version-control system many developers use. Nothing is ever really overwritten: open History to see every past version and restore one if you need to."}}</p>
    <div class="admin-links">
        <a href="/history">{{T "History"}}</a>
    </div>

    <h2>{{T "Chat"}}</h2>
    <p>{{T "A running stream of thoughts - global, or attached to a single file. Unlike your notes, chat messages aren't saved as part of a file, they're kept separately."}}</p>
    <div class="admin-links">
        <a href="/chat">{{T "Chat"}}</a>
    </div>

    <h2>{{T "Kanban"}}</h2>
    <p>{{T "Track files as cards moving through stages, e.g. inbox to in progress to done. It's not a separate system - a card is just a file with a status tag, so it's still the same file everywhere else in the app. Configure boards in Settings."}}</p>
    <div class="admin-links">
        <a href="/kanban">{{T "Kanban"}}</a>
    </div>

    <h2>{{T "Settings & Admin"}}</h2>
    <p>{{T "Settings controls how the app looks and behaves for you. Admin covers maintenance for the whole app."}}</p>
    <div class="admin-links">
        <a href="/settings">{{T "Settings"}}</a>
        <a href="/admin">{{T "Admin"}}</a>
    </div>
    <p>{{T "Want to try the app out without using your real notes? Fill it with sample files."}}</p>
    <p>{{T "Sample files are set up automatically on the very first start. Use Clean Test Data below if you want to remove them."}}</p>
    <div class="admin-action-list">
        <button class="btn-secondary" hx-post="/api/testdata/setup" hx-swap="none"
                hx-confirm="{{T "Setup test data? This will create example files in the data/test folder."}}">
            {{T "Setup Test Data"}}
        </button>
        <button class="btn-danger" hx-post="/api/testdata/clean" hx-swap="none"
                hx-confirm="{{T "This will remove all files in the data/test Folder."}}">
            {{T "Clean Test Data"}}
        </button>
    </div>
</div>
{{ end }}
